$ jailops firewall address-set create office --address 192.0.2.0/24 --comment the office
address set/office created

$ jailops firewall policy create web --comment the web server
firewall policy/web created

$ jailops firewall rule add web in --action allow --proto tcp --from any --port 80 --comment the site
firewall policy/web: rule 1 added: allow in tcp from any port 80
! note: this lets the Internet in; jailops expose does the same and also adds the IPv4 forward

$ jailops firewall rule add web in --action allow --proto tcp --from ::/0 --port 443 --comment the site over IPv6
firewall policy/web: rule 2 added: allow in tcp from ::/0 port 443
! note: this lets the Internet in; jailops expose does the same and also adds the IPv4 forward

$ jailops firewall rule add web in --action allow --proto tcp --from set:office --port 22 --comment ssh from the office
firewall policy/web: rule 3 added: allow in tcp from set:office port 22
! note: the rule opens the uplink of the jails with this policy that have a routed address, from set:office (review: jailops firewall show JAIL)

$ jailops firewall rule edit web 3 --from 0.0.0.0/0
firewall policy/web: rule 3 changed: allow in tcp from 0.0.0.0/0 port 22
! note: this lets the Internet in; jailops expose does the same and also adds the IPv4 forward

$ jailops firewall rule edit web 3 --from set:office
firewall policy/web: rule 3 changed: allow in tcp from set:office port 22

$ jailops firewall rule add web out --action allow --proto tcp --to any --port 443 --comment outbound is not it
firewall policy/web: rule 4 added: allow out tcp to any port 443

